{{!--
  Pipeline diagram template ("19 §19.1's own "pipeline diagrams" row) -- renders the already-registered
  `Diagram` type (@forge/schemas' own registry) around a real Mermaid flowchart produced by
  @forge/diagrams' own already-real `pipelineToFlow` generator (packages/diagrams/src/generate/
  generators.ts), per module.yaml's own header comment: no new generator or artifact type was needed.

  `source`/`depicts`/`generator` below are NOT authored by hand -- a real caller runs `pipelineToFlow`
  first and passes its own `GeneratedDiagram.source`/`.depicts` straight into this template's context,
  matching the Diagram schema's own "generated: true requires a generator" rule
  (@forge/schemas/artifacts/diagram.ts). See test/fm-data-templates.test.ts for the real, end-to-end
  proof (a real pipeline stage fixture -> pipelineToFlow -> this template -> diagramSchema).

  `sourceJson` (front matter) vs `rawSource` (the fenced code block in the body) are deliberately two
  separate context fields carrying the identical Mermaid text: `pipelineToFlow`'s own real output is a
  multi-line string ("flowchart LR\n  a --> b\n..."), and no 19 §19.2 `{{indent n text}}` helper is
  registered anywhere in this repository yet (the same "no custom helper exists" constraint every other
  real .hbs template here already documents) to fold a raw multi-line value into a YAML block scalar
  safely. `sourceJson` is the caller-supplied `JSON.stringify(generatedDiagram.source)` -- a valid,
  already-escaped inline YAML/JSON double-quoted scalar, newlines included -- while `rawSource` is the
  same text unescaped, safe to place inside a fenced Markdown code block in the body (outside the YAML
  front matter entirely).

  `fence` is ALSO caller-computed, not a hard-coded ` ```mermaid `/` ``` ` pair: a critic round found
  that a hard-coded triple-backtick fence around a caller-controlled `rawSource` is not safe against a
  pipeline stage name containing three or more literal backticks (`@forge/diagrams`' own
  `sanitizeMermaidLabel` only ever escapes `"`, never a backtick -- confirmed directly against
  packages/diagrams/src/generate/sanitize.ts) -- such a stage name would prematurely close the fence
  and let arbitrary Markdown/structure leak into the rendered document body. The real caller computes
  `fence` as a run of backticks one longer than the longest run of consecutive backticks anywhere in
  `rawSource` (minimum three, the ordinary case), the standard CommonMark "fenced code block" escaping
  rule -- see test/fm-data-templates.test.ts for the real regression fixture (a stage name containing
  four literal backticks).

  Renders against 19 §19.2's own real TemplateContext shape, the same convention warehouse-model.md.hbs
  documents. Only Handlebars built-in helpers are used (#each, #if).
--}}
---
id: {{{artifact.id}}}
type: Diagram
schemaVersion: 1
title: {{{title}}}
status: {{{status}}}
created: {{{now}}}
updated: {{{now}}}
revision: 1
author: {{{artifact.author}}}
changelog:
  - revision: 1
    date: {{{now}}}
    by: {{{artifact.author}}}
    summary: {{{changelogSummary}}}
kind: {{{kind}}}
notation: mermaid
source: {{{sourceJson}}}
generated: true
generator: {{{generator}}}
depicts:
{{#each depicts}}
  - {{{this}}}
{{else}}
  []
{{/each}}
explains:
{{#each explains}}
  - {{{this}}}
{{else}}
  []
{{/each}}
caption: {{{caption}}}
alt_text: {{{altText}}}
owner: {{{artifact.author}}}
---

